3. Secondary benefits
    • Thermal margin: lower copper losses reduce winding temperature rise, extending life.
    • Voltage ripple: less current ripple → smaller required capacitor bank for the same ΔV.
    • Control stability: torque-per-amp linearity improves at moderate loading, so phase-tracking loops stay quieter.

4. How to phrase this in your report
Although the DE5 1×1 exhibits substantially higher peak torque capability, its greater headroom allows operation in the high-efficiency zone for the same mechanical demand.
Consequently, energy consumption per kilometer decreases and effective range increases — the additional power capacity is not wasted, but leveraged to operate the drive more efficiently.

